# Experiment trace retention

- Treat success, failure, timeout and launch error as equally recordable runs.
- Write every run under `experiment/<name>/runs/<run-id>`; never put generated
  experiment state in `env/`.
- Preserve `agent/events.jsonl`, `agent/session.jsonl` when available, prompt,
  stderr, RoboEnv run metadata, native evidence and stop status.
- Call `experiment/lib/finalize_run.py` from an `EXIT` trap after stopping the
  simulator. Do not make HTML generation conditional on `native_success`.
- Every run must contain `trace-manifest.json`, `trace.html` and
  `trace-render.log`. A renderer failure must produce a fallback HTML and must
  not delete or rewrite raw traces.
- Use RoboTwin `native_success`, not the model's prose, as the success label.
- Keep observable model inputs/outputs and tool calls/results in the report;
  raw JSONL remains the authoritative record.
